# The `tabular-center::no-static-entry` fixture: a state no run can reach.
#
# `Jammed` is declared, has a row, and can even be left -- but no cell in the
# matrix transitions into it, and `Closed` is the initial state. In a matrix
# that is FULLY static that is a proof, not a guess: there is no HANDLE whose
# body might go there, so the state is dead code.
#
# The fully-static gate is the point. `effects-never.tbl` pins the other side
# of it -- `Open` there is reached only from a HANDLE, and the lint must stay
# silent. This fixture has no HANDLE, no DELEGATE and no UNREACHABLE at all, so
# the gate opens and the lint must speak. The two together pin the gate from
# both directions.
#
# The second thing it pins: `Jammed`'s own EMIT(Thud) is `stay` plus an
# effect, not a transition into `Jammed`. An implementation that counted an
# EMIT as a self-GO would find an incoming edge here and stay silent.
#
# Quiet elsewhere: every row has a GO, so no `no-static-exit` and no `dead-row`;
# every column has a live cell; 5 of 9 IGNORE is 55%; no UNREACHABLE; no
# payloads.

machine Door
initial Closed
states  Closed Open Jammed
actions Push Pull Kick

Closed | GO(Open)   | IGNORE     | IGNORE
Open   | IGNORE     | GO(Closed) | IGNORE
Jammed | EMIT(Thud) | IGNORE     | GO(Closed)
